{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>I also will do this unto you.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): 'I will punish you thus,' for the measures of the Holy One, blessed be He, are measure for measure. Just as you sinned with seven transgressions that He mentioned, so I will punish you with seven calamities that terrify you." "<b>Consumption and fever</b> — these are two. And lest they suppose in their hearts that they would survive these plagues, Scripture says <b>consuming the eyes and languishing the soul</b>, meaning that they would die from them — these are three." "<b>And you shall sow your seed in vain and your enemies shall eat it</b> — these are four. 'And I will set My face against you and you shall be smitten' — these are five. 'And your enemies shall rule over you' — these are six. 'And you shall flee with none pursuing you' — these are seven calamities. And from this Scripture says: 'seven for your sins,' meaning seven calamities for your sins, which are seven. And He mentioned yet again seven other calamities, and these are they: 'And I will break the pride of your power' — this is the Holy Temple, as it says (Ezekiel 24:21): 'Behold, I profane My sanctuary, the pride of your power' — this is one. 'Your heavens like iron' — these are two. 'Your land like bronze' — these are three. 'And it shall be in vain' — these are four. 'And your land shall not yield' — these are five. 'And the tree of the land shall not give' — these are six. 'Its fruit' — these are seven. For the word 'shall not give' serves for both of them: the tree shall not give and the fruit shall not give, and there you have seven calamities. And He mentioned yet a third time seven other calamities, and these are they: 'And I will send the beast of the field among you' — and it is one, and includes three: the provoking of beast, the provoking of animal, the provoking of the rest of creeping things, as it is written (Deuteronomy 32:24–25): 'I will send the tooth of beasts against them, with the venom of creeping things of the dust,' and 'it shall bereave you' — these are four. 'And cut you off' — these are five. 'And make you few' — these are six. 'And your roads shall be desolate' — these are seven. And He mentioned yet a fourth time seven other calamities, and they are: 'a sword avenging the vengeance of the covenant' — this is one. 'And you shall be gathered to your cities' — these are two. 'And I will send pestilence' — these are three. 'And you shall be delivered into the hand of the enemy' — this is the sword He mentioned; 'When I break for you the staff of bread' — these are four. 'And ten women shall bake your bread in one oven' — these are five. 'And they shall return your bread' — these are six. 'And you shall eat and not be satisfied' — these are seven. And He mentioned yet a fifth time seven other calamities: eating the flesh of sons and daughters — this is one. The destruction of the high places and the cutting down of the sun-images — these are two, for through the destruction of the high places the sun-images fall, and the essence of idolatry is called 'sun-images' (חמנים) because it is made for the sake of the constellations of the sun. 'And I will give your carcasses' — these are three. 'And My soul shall abhor you' — this is the departure of the Shekhinah — these are four. 'Your cities shall be desolate' — these are five. 'The desolation of the Sanctuary from the battalions' — these are six. 'And I will not smell the savor of your sweet odors' — these are seven. 'And I will bring the land into desolation' — this is not a calamity but a measure of good for Israel, that the enemies should find no gratification in the land." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'I also will do this unto you' — the word 'I' (אני) alludes to the attribute of Judgment, and so too in every other occurrence of אני. From this the Ramban, of blessed memory, said that it is as though it were inverted: 'אף אני זאת אעשה לכם,' to explain that the word 'I' (אני) is the attribute called זאת, and this זאת is the final הא that chastises a person in the time of anger. Therefore it says ויסרתי ליסרה אתכם — with the addition of the הא — and it did not say ליסר. And the meaning of ויספתי is: 'I will give increase in the attribute of Judgment, which is the הא of ליסרה אתכם,' for in the First Temple these rebukes were present, and there was the attribute of Tiferet and Glory. And so the Prophet said further (Isaiah 64:10): 'Our holy and beautiful house.' And similar to this (Genesis 8:21): לא אוסיף לקלל, whose meaning is 'I will not give increase in the attribute of Judgment to curse anymore.' And this is the intercessor and the overseer (הסרסור והאדריכל) that they, of blessed memory, mentioned in the Midrash in Bereshit Rabbah, and it is that which draws Him near in the time of will and does battle on behalf against His enemies. And concerning it David, of blessed memory, said (Psalms 27:3): 'Though war arise against me, in this (בזאת) I trust.' And so the Prophet said (Malachi 3:7): 'Return to Me and I will return to you' — it was not said אשוב but אשובה. And this is the meaning of ויסרתי אתכם אף אני — it is not enough that I am the Master of Judgment, but 'I also' (אף אני) will chastise. Up to here. And what He said, 'seven for your sins' — the attribute called זאת, which is the one that says ויסרתי והכיתי, is also called 'seven' (שבע) and 'Bat-Sheva' (בת שבע), and she was the mother of Solomon, and this is (Isaiah 50:1): 'and for your transgressions your mother was sent away' (שולחה אמכם), and this is clear."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:00.558617804Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}